WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Where do your AI coding hours go? Prompt Analytics shows you, locally.

00:03.000 --> 00:08.500
Totals, trend and what needs attention, at a glance.

00:08.500 --> 00:11.500
Which assistant handles which kind of work: the router matrix.

00:11.500 --> 00:14.700
Activity calendar and hour of week.

00:14.700 --> 00:17.900
Flip it to 3D, then drag to orbit.

00:17.900 --> 00:20.300
Same data, new angle.

00:20.300 --> 00:23.100
Hour of week, flat.

00:23.100 --> 00:25.600
Or as a 3D terrain of your working rhythm.

00:25.600 --> 00:29.400
Where prompts stall, and which tool switches follow.

00:29.400 --> 00:33.400
Friction by tool and by intent.

00:33.400 --> 00:36.600
The loop breaker flags retry loops.

00:36.600 --> 00:39.600
A playbook distilled from the prompts that succeeded.

00:39.600 --> 00:43.800
Secrets and PII are found and masked, never stored raw.

00:43.800 --> 00:47.000
Every session in a table. Page ten rows, or more.

00:47.000 --> 00:49.800
Twenty-five rows. Switch density to fit more.

00:49.800 --> 00:52.000
Compact rows.

00:52.000 --> 00:54.300
Export what you see.

00:54.300 --> 00:56.800
CSV, JSON or xlsx.

00:56.800 --> 01:00.300
A 3D mind map of your topics.

01:00.300 --> 01:03.100
Only use one assistant? The dashboard adapts.

01:03.100 --> 01:05.900
Sections reshape to your tool.

01:05.900 --> 01:08.900
Press Cmd+K to jump anywhere.

01:08.900 --> 01:12.900
Know where your hours go. Run uvx prompt-analytics run.
